# __PLUGIN_PKG__

__DESCRIPTION__

A plugin for [SignalRange](https://github.com/thkruz/SignalRange). It registers
one antenna (`__ANTENNA_ID__`) that shows up in every sandbox loadout.

## Develop

The plugin needs the SignalRange engine to compile against. Two common setups:

**A. Develop inside a SignalRange checkout (recommended)**

```bash
git clone https://github.com/thkruz/SignalRange
cd SignalRange
pnpm install
pnpm run plugin -- create my-plugin      # scaffolds src/plugins-external/signal-range-plugin-my-plugin
pnpm run plugin -- dev __PLUGIN_ID__     # boots a sandbox with only this plugin, live-reload
```

Edit the files under `src/plugins-external/__PLUGIN_PKG__/`, then push them to
their own git repo (`git remote add origin …` from inside the plugin folder).

**B. Develop standalone**

Clone this repo next to a `SignalRange` checkout (so the `../SignalRange` paths
in `tsconfig.json` resolve), or clone SignalRange into `.signal-range/`. Then
`pnpm install` here for editor type-checking.

## Install (for users)

```bash
# From a SignalRange checkout:
pnpm run plugin -- add __REPO_URL__
pnpm run build   # or restart `pnpm run dev`
```

## Try it

Open any campaign sandbox, click **LOADOUT** in the command bar, and pick the
antenna. To skip the picker, append `?antenna=__ANTENNA_ID__` to the sandbox URL.

## The two hard rules

1. The entry (`src/plugin.ts`) must have a **named export** matching `className`
   in `signal-range-plugin.json` (`__CLASS_NAME__`).
2. The class's `readonly id` must **equal** the manifest's plugin `id`
   (`__PLUGIN_ID__`).

